  "worked_solution": "First, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x]_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{e}^{4}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{e}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}{y}^{2}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}}2{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\frac{2}{3}[{y}^{3}]_{0}^{\\sqrt[3]{6}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}((\\sqrt[3]{6})^{3}-{0}^{3}) \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
